  "_note": "One saved response from the news database query, kept so the transform in sync-news-notion.py can be run without a token: python3 scripts/sync-news-notion.py --fixture scripts/data/notion-news.sample.json --dry-run. Three rows on purpose — one published with every optional field, one published with none, and one Entwurf that must not reach the site. `_blocks` is this script's own field and not Notion's: the page bodies come from a second request per published row, and saving them beside the row is what lets the whole transform — properties and text — run against a file. The third row's blocks carry one of everything the reading page has a form for, plus a video, which has none and must be reported rather than dropped in silence. There is deliberately NO image block here: a picture is downloaded, so a fixture with one would need the network and this file exists to be run without it."
